plugin-hostd (0.11.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * release: plugin-hostd 0.11.0
  * packaging: omx-clap-core 0.21.0 the floor, the release whose
    omx-clap-host runs a chain in one client
  * fuzz_command: the reply-answer record cites verbs.c:220, the line
    chain_get's branch moved by six (#162)
  * fuzz/README: the reply answer, the broadcast arity, the words worked out,
    the no-loss of what was written (#159)
  * fuzz/sabotage: each patch's header names the line of its check in the
    harness as it is now (#159)
  * fuzz: the no-loss check holds the relay to every byte a worker wrote
    before a read or a removal (#159)
  * fuzz: the words check works out the placement, the client, the chain
    members and the verdict from the message (#159)
  * fuzz: the arity check holds a verb the daemon broadcasts to its declared
    count too (#159)
  * fuzz: the reply check holds a reply to the answer of the call that
    answered, else to the daemon's own (#159)
  * fuzz/sabotage: a patch may name a part of a property, and is caught in
    that part or in the property (#159)
  * fuzz_command: five records cite the verbs.c lines chain_get's branch
    moved by six (#162)
  * sabotage: the four arms that quote replay, chain_form and the order's
    replay follow their moved text (#162)
  * chain: members of clap and lv2-clap, two rows of omx-clap-host, form one
    chain on the adapter row (#162)
  * chain: a chain declared again while its worker is up keeps that worker, a
    joining member replayed into it (#162)
  * supervisor: a replay by instance, its add, its ledger, its connections,
    and chain_formed, one function each (#162)
  * chain_get: a chain read back, its worker, its members as declared and the
    ones its worker runs (#162)
  * protocol.h: chain_get declared, chain's re-declaration in place and its
    one-program rule, the README and protocol JSON regenerated (#162)
  * chains note: chain_get reads a chain back, a chain declared again keeps
    its running worker, clap and lv2-clap members form one chain (#162)
  * fuzz: the command harness's coverage floor rises to the 155 lines its
    corpus covers (#159)
  * fuzz/README: the records, the words property, the patches in
    fuzz/sabotage (#159)
  * fuzz: make fuzz-records meets every record, and a check with none is
    refused (#159)
  * fuzz_command: each call takes the message's words where its verb declares
    them (#159)
  * fuzz: every check names the one-line change and the seed that make it
    abort (#159)
  * fuzz: the mutant patches move to fuzz/sabotage, each naming its check and
    seed (#159)

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 03:51:23 +0000
